# Half-slope stubs - way terminates on the slope's low / high edge,
# sprite covers only the half of the tile near that edge.  Baked by
# scene.py::bake_pakset() into rail_060_tracks_hex_slope_half.png:
# 6x2 grid, row 0 = low halves, row 1 = high halves, columns in
# SLOPE_HEX_HALF_ENTRIES axis order (n, ne, se, s, sw, nw).  Narrow
# and wide share cells exactly like the full crossing atlas above
# (the way's chord geometry is identical; off-axis terrain differs).
# No `_double` keys: rail_060 ships no double-slope art today.
ImageUp[n_low_half][0]=rail_060_tracks_hex_slope_half.0.0
ImageUp[ne_low_half][0]=rail_060_tracks_hex_slope_half.0.1
